      {
       "data": "Out[39]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{hw weights of V (x) V} & \\begin{pmatrix}2 & 2 & 2\\\\3 & 2 & 1\\\\3 & 3 & 0\\\\4 & 1 & 1\\\\4 & 2 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{\\# hw states per weight} & \\left\\{1,2,1,1,1\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{<v\\_tot (x) vacL | singlet> at a sample point (should be 0 exactly)} & 0\\\\\\hline\\text{limitSpanS test: rows (1, $\\varepsilon$), (1, 2$\\varepsilon$) -> limit spans} & \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1\\\\1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "8b2415e9-6a08-4adf-b755-9ceeb20f1aa2"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 3. Families. base = <v_tot (x) vacL| over random (k1, k2, p1, p2); t_λ family = base . t_λ(x) with a random x per sample.\n   Every family is torus-covariant (the Cartan rescales p1, p2 compatibly with the vacL relation; t_λ commutes with the total Cartan),\n   so its span splits into total-weight sectors of V (x) V, and the limit is taken sector by sector (dim <= 10 instead of 64).\n   Sample sufficiency, per family and sector: the rank at a random ε is the same with 80 and with all nS samples. ---- *)\nClearAll[rqS, nS, parS, xS, famS, labsS, setsS, secS, stabS, limS, timeS];\nSeedRandom[20260923];\nrqS[] := RandomChoice[{-1, 1}] RandomInteger[{2, 40}] / RandomInteger[{3, 29}];\nnS = 120;\nparS = Table[{rqS[], rqS[], rqS[], rqS[]}, nS];\nxS = Table[rqS[], nS];\nlabsS = {{1, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 0}, {2, 1}};\nfamS = <|\"base\" -> (baseS /@ parS)|>;\nDo[famS[lab] = MapThread[tfActS[#1, lab, #2] &, {famS[\"base\"], xS}], {lab, labsS}];\n\nsetsS = <|\"base\" -> {\"base\"}, Table[\"base + t\" <> ToString[lab] -> {\"base\", lab}, {lab, labsS}], \"base + all four\" -> Keys[famS]|>;\nsecS[nu_] := Flatten @ Position[wt2S, nu];\nstabS = Table[With[{r = famS[f][[All, secS[nu]]] /. ε -> 5/13}, {MatrixRank[r[[;; 80]]], MatrixRank[r], Length[secS[nu]]}], {f, Keys[famS]}, {nu, hwWtsS}];\n\n(* per set and hw weight: rank of lim span (sector) paired with the hw vectors of that weight *)\ntimeS = First @ AbsoluteTiming[\n    limS = Association @ Table[s -> Table[With[{L = limitSpanS[(Join @@ famS /@ setsS[s])[[All, secS[nu]]]]},\n        If[L === {}, 0, MatrixRank[L . Transpose[hwS[nu][[All, secS[nu]]]]]]], {nu, hwWtsS}], {s, Keys[setsS]}]];\n\nColumn[{\n    Grid[Prepend[MapThread[Prepend, {Map[Row[#, \" / \"] &, stabS, {2}], Keys[famS]}], Join[{\"family: rank(80) / rank(\" <> ToString[nS] <> \") / sector dim\"}, Row[#, \",\"] & /@ hwWtsS]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n    Grid[{{\"samples sufficient everywhere\", And @@ Flatten[Map[#[[1]] == #[[2]] &, stabS, {2}]]}, {\"time for all limits (s)\", timeS}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n    Grid[Prepend[KeyValueMap[Join[{#1}, #2, {Total[#2]}] &, limS],\n        Join[{\"family\"}, Row[#, \",\"] & /@ hwWtsS, {\"hw total (of 6)\"}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
