      }
     ],
     "id": "aba7ecef-dd46-4aa5-b0f9-1df1ee2acdd4"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 4b. The {n, m} singlet table of the SoV covectors (~3.5 min; results summarised in the next markdown cell). ---- *)\nClearAll[sovTabS, rank64S];\n(* two independent vacL choices; table entries {n, m} *)\nsovTabS = Table[With[{vac = vacS @@ pp},\n    Table[With[{xv = sovS[vac, g1, g2]}, {Min[ordRS /@ DeleteCases[xv, 0]], ordRS[xv . sngS]}], {g1, gtS}, {g2, gtS}]], {pp, {{3/5, 4/7}, {-7/4, 9/11}}}];\nrank64S = MatrixRank[Flatten[Table[sovS[vacS[3/5, 4/7], g1, g2], {g1, gtS}, {g2, gtS}], 1] /. ε -> 3/7];\n\nColumn[{\n    Grid[{{\"rank of the 64 SoV covectors at ε = 3/7\", rank64S}, {\"same {n, m} table for both vacL choices\", sovTabS[[1]] === sovTabS[[2]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n    Grid[Prepend[MapThread[Prepend, {Map[If[#[[2]] === Infinity, \"≡ 0\", If[#[[2]] == #[[1]], Style[\"YES\", Bold], Row[{\"+\", #[[2]] - #[[1]]}]]] &, sovTabS[[1]], {2}], Row[Flatten[#], \",\"] & /@ gtS}],\n        Prepend[Row[Flatten[#], \",\"] & /@ gtS, \"site 1 \\\\ site 2\"]], Frame -> All]\n}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (cell 8, exact; identical for two vacL choices)\n\n- The 64 covectors have rank 64 at finite twist ($\\varepsilon=3/7$), so they are a basis.\n- **No SoV covector has a singlet component in the limit.** Every covector has overall order $n=0$, i.e. a finite nonzero limit. The singlet overlap is:\n  - **identically zero** (at finite twist) for 54 of the 64 labels;\n  - $O(\\varepsilon^4)$ for the 10 label pairs whose label sums add to 6: $100|221,\\ 110|211,\\ 110|220,\\ 111|111,\\ 200|220,\\ 210|210,\\ 211|110,\\ 220|110,\\ 220|200,\\ 221|100$ (written $n_{21}n_{11}n_{12}$ per site). These are exactly the 10 labels of the singlet's weight sector.\n- **Why: the whole basis collapses.** The 64 limit covectors have **rank 1**, all proportional to $\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}\\otimes\\mathrm{vacL}|$ at $\\varepsilon=0$. At $z=1$, $\\mathrm{vacL}\\otimes\\mathrm{vacL}$ is a rotated hw covector of the multiplicity-one irrep $[4,2,0]$, and the untwisted $t_\\lambda$ are gl(3)-invariant, so they act on it as scalars. Every SoV covector is therefore (vacuum) $+\\,O(\\varepsilon)$, and the singlet only shows up in differences of basis covectors, at relative order $\\varepsilon^4$.\n- So \"singlet component of an individual SoV covector in the limit\" is empty. The meaningful object is the limit of the span (or a rescaled triangular recombination of the basis). The span of all 64 covectors trivially contains the singlet; which recombination carries it at $\\varepsilon^4$ is the next question.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Undo $g_0\\otimes g_0$, project to a weight space, then expand\n\nThe twist is diagonal, so every eigenstate $\\Psi_A$ has a definite total weight $\\nu$. It pairs only with the $\\nu$-component of a covector, and $\\Psi_A$ can diverge as a different power of $\\varepsilon$ in different sectors. So the expansion is done **per total-weight sector**, and **per covector**:\n$$u_x=\\langle x|(g_0^{-1}\\otimes g_0^{-1}),\\qquad u_{x,\\nu}=P_\\nu u_x=\\varepsilon^{o_{x,\\nu}}\\big(\\ell_{x,\\nu}+O(\\varepsilon)\\big).$$\n$g_0$ is $\\varepsilon$-independent on the linear curve. $u_x$ is computed as an exact series truncated at $\\varepsilon^K$, with $t_{\\{1,0\\}}^{-1}$ expanded as a Neumann series around its invertible $\\varepsilon=0$ block. Whether a sector projection vanishes identically is checked separately, exactly, at $\\varepsilon=3/7$ without truncation.\n\nThe target $(e_1^TP)\\otimes e_1^T$ has $\\nu$-component $w\\otimes e_1^T$ with $w$ in the site-1 weight space $\\mu=\\nu-(2,1,0)$. So in each sector we ask for $\\dim\\big(\\mathrm{span}\\{\\ell_{x,\\nu}\\}\\cap V_\\mu\\otimes e_1^T\\big)$ compared with $\\dim V_\\mu$. The singlet sector is $\\nu=(2,2,2)$, which needs $\\mu=(0,1,2)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 5. u_x = <x| (g0^-1 (x) g0^-1) as exact series to ε^K; per total-weight sector ν: leading order o_{x,ν} and vector l_{x,ν};\n   overlap of span{l_{x,ν}} with V_μ (x) e1^T, μ = ν - (2,1,0). Exact-zero test at ε = 3/7 without truncation. ---- *)\nClearAll[KS, truncS, a0InvOKS, invSerS, opSerS, opNumS, gMatS, vac1S, vacNumS, Ginv2S, uS, uNumS, wt1S, secDataS, rowsS, timeUS];\nKS = 8;\ntruncS[e_] := Expand[e] /. ε^n_ /; n > KS -> 0;\na0InvOKS = And @@ Flatten @ Table[MatrixRank[tfBlkS[{1, 0}, th, idx] /. ε -> 0] == Length[idx], {th, thS}, {idx, secListS}];\n(* A^-1 = A0^-1 sum_n (-R A0^-1)^n, R = A - A0 = O(ε) *)\ninvSerS[x_, idx_] := invSerS[x, idx] = Module[{A = tfBlkS[{1, 0}, x, idx], A0, A0i, M, P, S},\n    A0 = A /. ε -> 0; A0i = Inverse[A0]; M = truncS[-(A - A0) . A0i];\n    P = IdentityMatrix[Length[idx]]; S = P;\n    Do[P = truncS[P . M]; S = S + P, {KS}];\n    truncS[A0i . S]];\nopSerS[g_, x_, idx_] := opSerS[g, x, idx] = truncS @ Switch[g,\n    {{1}, {0, 0}}, IdentityMatrix[Length[idx]],\n    {{1}, {1, 0}}, tfBlkS[{1, 0}, x, idx],\n    {{1}, {1, 1}}, tfBlkS[{1, 1}, x, idx],\n    {{2}, {0, 0}}, tfBlkS[{2, 0}, x, idx] . invSerS[x, idx],\n    {{2}, {1, 0}}, tfBlkS[{2, 0}, x, idx],\n    {{2}, {1, 1}}, truncS[tfBlkS[{2, 0}, x, idx] . invSerS[x, idx]] . tfBlkS[{1, 1}, x, idx],\n    {{2}, {2, 0}}, truncS[tfBlkS[{2, 0}, x, idx] . invSerS[x, idx]] . tfBlkS[{2, 0}, x, idx],\n    {{2}, {2, 1}}, truncS[tfBlkS[{2, 0}, x, idx] . invSerS[x, idx]] . tfBlkS[{2, 1}, x, idx]];\n(* exact operator at a numeric ε, for the exact-zero test *)\nopNumS[g_, x_, idx_, e0_] := With[{t = tfBlkS[#, x, idx] /. ε -> e0 &}, Switch[g,\n    {{1}, {0, 0}}, IdentityMatrix[Length[idx]], {{1}, {1, 0}}, t[{1, 0}], {{1}, {1, 1}}, t[{1, 1}],\n    {{2}, {0, 0}}, t[{2, 0}] . Inverse[t[{1, 0}]], {{2}, {1, 0}}, t[{2, 0}],\n    {{2}, {1, 1}}, t[{2, 0}] . Inverse[t[{1, 0}]] . t[{1, 1}], {{2}, {2, 0}}, t[{2, 0}] . Inverse[t[{1, 0}]] . t[{2, 0}],\n    {{2}, {2, 1}}, t[{2, 0}] . Inverse[t[{1, 0}]] . t[{2, 1}]]];\n\nWith[{p1 = 3/5, p2 = 4/7}, With[{p3 = Together[p2 (zS[[3]] - zS[[1]]) / (p1 (zS[[2]] - zS[[3]]))]},\n    gMatS = expNS[p1 Normal[ES[1, 2]]] . expNS[p2 Normal[ES[1, 3]]] . expNS[p3 Normal[ES[2, 3]]]]];\nvac1S = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[dS, 1] . gMatS, UnitVector[dS, 1] . gMatS]];\nGinv2S = KroneckerProduct[Inverse[gMatS], Inverse[gMatS]];\n\ntimeUS = First @ AbsoluteTiming[\n    uS = Flatten[Table[Module[{out = ConstantArray[0, dcS]},\n        Do[out[[idx]] = truncS[truncS[vac1S[[idx]] . opSerS[g1, thS[[1]], idx]] . opSerS[g2, thS[[2]], idx]], {idx, secListS}];\n        truncS[out . Ginv2S]], {g1, gtS}, {g2, gtS}], 1];\n    uNumS = Flatten[Table[Module[{out = ConstantArray[0, dcS]},\n        Do[out[[idx]] = (vac1S[[idx]] /. ε -> 3/7) . opNumS[g1, thS[[1]], idx, 3/7] . opNumS[g2, thS[[2]], idx, 3/7], {idx, secListS}];\n        out . (Ginv2S /. ε -> 3/7)], {g1, gtS}, {g2, gtS}], 1]];\n\n(* site-1 weights; per sector ν: {o, l} per covector; \"Z\" = exactly zero, \"K\" = zero through ε^K but not exactly *)\nwt1S = Transpose[Table[Diagonal[Normal[ES[i, i]]], {i, 3}]];\nsecDataS[nu_] := Module[{idx = Flatten @ Position[wt2S, nu], mu = nu - repS, ent, fin, os, L, Lmin, Vmu, cap},\n    ent = Table[With[{c = uS[[x, idx]]},\n        If[Union[c] === {0}, If[Union[uNumS[[x, idx]]] === {0}, \"Z\", \"K\"],\n            With[{o = Min[Exponent[#, ε, Min] & /@ DeleteCases[c, 0]]}, {o, Coefficient[#, ε, o] & /@ c}]]], {x, 64}];\n    fin = Cases[ent, {_Integer, _List}];\n    os = fin[[All, 1]];\n    L = fin[[All, 2]];\n    Lmin = If[fin === {}, {}, Pick[L, Thread[os == Min[os]]]];\n    (* V_mu (x) e1^T inside the sector, as vectors on idx *)\n    Vmu = Table[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[dS, n1], UnitVector[dS, 1]]][[idx]], {n1, Flatten @ Position[wt1S, mu]}];\n    cap[S_] := If[S === {} || Vmu === {}, 0, MatrixRank[S] + MatrixRank[Vmu] - MatrixRank[Join[S, Vmu]]];\n    {nu, Length[idx], mu, Length[Vmu], Count[ent, \"Z\"], Count[ent, \"K\"], If[os === {}, \"-\", Min[os]], If[os === {}, \"-\", Sort[Tally[os]]],\n     If[L === {}, 0, MatrixRank[L]], cap[L], If[Lmin === {}, 0, MatrixRank[Lmin]], cap[Lmin]}];\nrowsS = secDataS /@ SortBy[Union[wt2S], -# . {100, 10, 1} &];\n\nColumn[{\n    Grid[{{\"ε=0 blocks of t_{1,0}(θ_s) invertible (Neumann series valid)\", a0InvOKS}, {\"time (s)\", timeUS},\n        {\"u_x(0) all ∝ e1 (x) e1\", MatrixRank[Append[uS /. ε -> 0, Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[dS, 1], UnitVector[dS, 1]]]]] == 1}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n    Grid[Prepend[rowsS, {\"sector ν\", \"dim\", \"μ = ν-(2,1,0)\", \"dim V_μ\", \"# ≡0\", \"# >K\", \"min order\", \"{order, #x}\", \"rank l (all)\", \"∩ V_μ⊗e1 (all)\", \"rank l (min order)\", \"∩ V_μ⊗e1 (min)\"}], Frame -> All]\n}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
